    <string name="webhook_guide_intro">Follow these steps to configure your Zammad installation to send real-time signals to the app when a ticket is updated.</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step1_body">1. Log in to your Zammad instance as an administrator.\n2. Navigate to Settings (the gear icon).\n3. Find and click on \"Webhooks\" in the left-hand menu.</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step1_title">Step 1: Navigate to Webhooks in Zammad</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step2_body">1. Click the \"Add New Webhook\" button.\n2. Give the webhook a clear name, for example, \"Android App Notifications\".\n3. In the \"URL\" field, paste the unique, personal URL you just copied from the app.\n4. Ensure that \"Active\" is checked.</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step2_title">Step 2: Create a New Webhook</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step3_body">A \"Trigger\" is an event in Zammad that should activate the webhook. For the best results, we recommend setting up triggers for the following events:\n\n- Ticket Created\n- Ticket Updated</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step3_title">Step 3: Configure Triggers</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step4_body">1. Click \"Save\" or \"Submit\".\n2. Zammad will send a \"ping\" to the URL to confirm it\'s working. You should see a success message in Zammad.</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_step4_title">Step 4: Save and Test</string>
    <string name="webhook_guide_title">Webhook Setup Guide</string>
